From 4a6b6756198b474eff7f6017ea38d8535c4de886 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bryan Hoban <bryan.hoban@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 14:40:40 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 08/14] yblod-engine-vk: bilinear FEL EL upscale (el_scaler 2)

A cheaper EL upscale for devices where CB1's Master Reference filter (CCM
Annex B: 8-tap horizontal, 4-tap vertical) is too expensive, e.g. the
Raspberry Pi 5: dvvk_plan_in.el_scaler 2.

Bilinear with Annex B's siting and rounding: the EL co-sited horizontally
(odd samples (a + b + 1) / 2), rows at 1/4 and 3/4 vertically
((3a + b + 2) / 4); the EL chroma keeps Annex B's chroma phase filter and
64/192 vertical step (already bilinear) and gets the 2-tap horizontal. To
yblod's host code bilinear is Annex B (tables, routes); only the shaders'
EL filter code (0 Annex B, 1 nearest, 2 bilinear) differs. Every EL site:
vertical_pair (+w32), horizontal(), luma_phase_guide, mmr_dual_horizontal,
fel_chroma, the fused FEL pack.

Checked on lavapipe: Annex B and nearest outputs byte-identical to before;
bilinear's fused pack equal to its staged reference route (DVVK_VERIFY,
120 frames x 2 FEL clips x both contracts); vs Annex B 64 dB PSNR
(nearest: 50.6 dB). Route model tests cover el_scaler 2.
